From 6bd69728073f423e6942da9d9ede8dbdda13761f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 20:17:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix wmic-missing on Win11 23H2+ via PowerShell
 Get-CimInstance fallback

The user's verification output showed 5 fields reading as
'(error: program not found)' (disk WMIC, baseboard, BIOS, BIOS version,
csproduct UUID). Windows 11 23H2 ships without wmic.exe, so every wmic
call fails with io::ErrorKind::NotFound and the spoof's effect cannot be
verified for those fields.

Fixes:

- New probe_with_fallback(): try wmic first; if it returns a missing
  sentinel or fails, run an equivalent 'Get-CimInstance' query via
  PowerShell (prefer pwsh 7, fall back to legacy powershell.exe).
  CREATE_NO_WINDOW flag keeps the console hidden.
- capture_windows() routes disk/baseboard/BIOS/BIOS-version/UUID probes
  through the new fallback.
- wmic_first_value() detects ErrorKind::NotFound explicitly and returns
  the same '(read failed)' sentinel the fallback recognizes (instead of
  the cryptic 'error: program not found' string).
- classify_pair() error note now mentions Win11 23H2 + PowerShell as a
  likely cause so users do not waste time elevating to Administrator
  when the actual issue is a missing wmic binary.
- New unchanged_field_explanation() helper documents the fields that
  the user routinely sees stay the same in-session (Volume serial = boot
  sector cached until reboot; Hostname = registry-only until reboot;
  MAC = NIC driver override often ignored by firmware). push_check now
  appends the explanation to the verification note so the output is
  self-documenting.
- Unit tests cover the helper coverage, the chained-note behaviour for
  unchanged fields, and confirm no note is appended on changed fields.
---
 HWIDTool/src/hwid_snapshot.rs | 153 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 146 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

